# Architecture

## Runtime

- Vite + React + strict TypeScript.
- One root `CakeProvider` in `src/App.tsx`.
- `styled-components` for prototype-specific composition.
- Cake& CSS custom properties for every visual value.
- `lucide-react` or exact exported Figma assets for icons.

## Structure

- `src/components/shell/`: Windows frame, title bar, sidebar, and command bar.
- `src/components/dashboard/`: Home dashboard cards and status visuals.
- `src/components/updates/`: the check-for-updates toast flow, its state
  machine, details dialog, and System update panel.
- `src/components/prototype/`: non-production scenario controls.
- `src/data/`: typed mock data, thresholds, and state fixtures.
- `src/assets/`: exact downloaded Figma assets.
- `src/styles/`: token-only layout and global prototype composition.
- `src/test/`: test setup and accessibility helpers.

## State flow

`App` owns the selected destination, scenario, carousel pages, and transient
feedback. It passes typed data and callbacks into presentational shell and
dashboard components. `AppShell` owns the sidebar collapsed state, because the
rail width and the workspace grid column must change together. No backend or
persistence is introduced in Phase 1.

The update flow is the one stateful feature with its own machine: `useUpdateFlow`
owns the phase, progress, and failure disclosure, and advances phases from a
single interval so no effect writes state synchronously. `App` holds only the
inputs the flow cannot own — whether the next scan should fail, and whether the
details dialog is open. Presentational pieces (`UpdateFlowToast`,
`SystemUpdatePanel`) receive the flow and render a phase.

## Design-system gaps

Figma-specific radial status gauges, pager dots, Windows caption controls, and
the OS Mica shell recipe may be composed locally only when Cake& has no exported
equivalent. Each local composition must use Cake& tokens and be documented.

`UpdateToast` is such a composition: Cake&'s complex `Toast` layout has no slot
between its header and footer rows, which the progress and More/Less update
frames require. It mirrors Cake&'s own complex toast — same Radix primitive,
tokens, and 480px width — and keeps Cake& `Button`, `IconButton`, and
`ProgressBar` inside. Prefer widening Cake& upstream over extending this copy.
